course: dictionary
lesson: 8550
title: Scaly: skin, scales and sorting animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scaly comes from scale, a small hard flat plate, plus -y, which means covered with or full of. So scaly means covered with scales. Look at the clues in «Reptiles have dry, scaly skin that keeps water in». Reptiles are animals like lizards and snakes, and their skin is dry and covered in scales, so scaly describes the skin.
explain: Scaly has a second meaning, about skin that is dry and flaky, like skin that is peeling. «Butterfly wings are covered in tiny scales that rub off easily» uses the first meaning. Dry skin in winter can feel scaly, which is the second meaning. The context tells you which one fits.
explain: Scaly is an adjective, so it describes a noun: scaly skin, a scaly tail, scaly legs. Its comparison is scalier and scaliest. Scientists use scales to sort animals into groups, and so do the stories: «In the films, raptors are... scaly» shows how writers use the word to describe a creature.
fact: Scaly is an adjective. It describes a noun, as in «scaly skin».
fact: Scaly means covered with scales, the small hard flat plates on fish, snakes and lizards.
fact: Scaly can also mean dry and flaky, like skin that is peeling.
fact: The comparison is scaly, scalier, scaliest.
fact: «Lepidoptera» is the name for butterflies and moths, and it means «scaly wings».
exercise: «Reptiles have dry, scaly skin that keeps water in.» What does scaly mean here? | Bright and shiny | *Covered with small hard plates, and dry | Soft and smooth like a baby | Wet and slippery like water
exercise: Which of these animals is covered with scales? | *Lizard | Feather | Cloud
exercise: Copy the describing word in «a scaly tail». | *scaly | tail | a
test: «Butterfly wings are covered in tiny scales that rub off easily.» What are butterfly wings covered in? | *Tiny scales | Sand | Feathers
test: Mum says, «My hands are scaly in winter.» What does she mean? | *Her hands are dry and flaky | Her hands are covered in fish scales | Her hands are shiny and new
exam: Which word completes the list: scaly, ___, scaliest? | scaler | *scalier | scalyer
